Would writing this in a more functional style where you can't make this kind of ordering mistake help? I'm not too familiar with underscore, but something like his:

``` javascript
return $q.all(promises)
  .then(function(resolutions) {
    return $q.resolve(
      _.unzip(
        _.zip(forms, resolutions).filter(function(formAndRes) {
          return formAndRes[1];
        })
      )[0]);
  });
```

or

``` javascript
return $q.all(promises)
  .then(function(resolutions) {
    return $q.resolve(_.reduce(_.zip(forms, resolutions), function(memo, formAndRes) {
      if (formAndRes[1]) {
        memo.push(formAndRes[0]);
      }
    }, []);
  });
```

